 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "The U.N. says the one point five limit is slipping away. Can this summit change that?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "COP thirty-one opens Monday in Antalya, Türkiye, and runs until November twentieth. Türkiye is the host and holds the presidency. Australia leads the negotiations. Climate Home News says it is the first summit facing a near-certain overshoot of one point five."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "The U.N. Environment Programme says current national pledges point to about two point six degrees of warming this century. Current policies point to about two point eight. UNEP says the chance of holding one point five without overshoot has been lost."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "Money is a main fault line. At COP thirty, countries agreed to call for efforts to triple adaptation finance to one hundred twenty billion dollars a year by twenty thirty-five. Climate Home News says developing countries want firm reassurances in Antalya."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will Antalya deliver more money for adaptation? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
